(5282724, 769204, 60173, '<td valign="top">I''m not voting, so this is just an observation...<br/> <br/>Put aside the challenge for a moment, and you''re left wondering why there''s binkies in the snow. Bring the challenge back and one''s got to wonder why bright green and pink are trying to pass themselves as "light" in the "Light on white" challenge.<br/> <br/>Put all of that aside and one has to admit you did control your light pretty well. Florescent colors tend to go "hot" really easily when even the slightest bit over exposed.</td>', 'I''m not voting, so this is just an observation... Put aside the challenge for a moment, and you''re left wondering why there''s binkies in the snow. Bring the challenge back and one''s got to wonder why bright green and pink are trying to pass themselves as "light" in the "Light on white" challenge. Put all of that aside and one has to admit you did control your light pretty well. Florescent colors tend to go "hot" really easily when even the slightest bit over exposed.', '2009-03-02 01:38:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5282726, 768571, 96915, '<td valign="top">Water droplets don''t hold much appeal for me, unless there''s something really unique to set them apart from the rest.  I''m afraid this one doesn''t really capture me as unique.</td>', 'Water droplets don''t hold much appeal for me, unless there''s something really unique to set them apart from the rest.  I''m afraid this one doesn''t really capture me as unique.', '2009-03-02 01:39:22.000000', NULL, 1),
